foreign  thousands of students from all over the  world hope to study in Nations other  than their own for a variety of reasons  many of them cite job advancement higher  pay and lifestyle changes as the reasons  for traveling to foreign countries  however making this decision of studying  abroad is not that easy you'll have to  carry out thorough research about which  country is best suited for you and what  prospects it has to offer and to assist  you with that we bring you this video on  best countries to study abroad in this  session we'll explore the factors that  are commonly referred to while choosing  the country to study abroad and after  that we'll look at the top four  countries for abroad education so make  sure you stay back until the end of this  video  first let's dive into the parameters for  selecting the best country for studying  abroad  education is the greatest transforming  instrument in the world shaping not just  individuals but also societies no matter  in which corner of the world we live in  education should be given Prime  importance as it help us gain new  knowledge progress in life and build a  better world for tomorrow education also  makes us think and behave more  rationally though education is  acknowledged and valued in Many Nations  throughout the world a few countries  stand out if we attempt to focus on what  constitutes the finest education system  in the world their education systems are  not only of great quality but many of  them also have certain distinguishing  features that set them apart for example  the United States is one of the most  popular destinations for students  worldwide the reason is high quality  education world-class faculty and  cutting-edge infrastructure and  Facilities according to Qs World  university ranking report the United  States is considered to have better  educational System since 28 universities  from this country rank among the top  hundred universities globally  the United Kingdom is the second best  country for Quality education 16  universities from United Kingdom rank in  top 100 universities worldwide the  institutions from the UK hold strong  brand identity University of Oxford  University of Cambridge Imperial College  of London University of Edinburgh London  School of economics and political  sciences hold a strong value in  education industry  the next factor that matters a lot is  the student acceptance rate this is one  of the foremost concern for students who  wish to study abroad everyone faces the  difficulty of assimilating into a  completely different environment culture  traditions and Customs despite putting  in a ton of efforts to become acquainted  with the culture acceptance remains a  major goal for individuals in recent  times students have become little  skeptical about countries such as  Australia UK and Italy the reason behind  this is the past event of racism and  anti-migrant sentiments according to a  survey done by human rights Department  in Australia 85 percent of respondents  believe that racism is the biggest  current issue in Australia you can  observe the same scenario in United  Kingdom as well events like brexit and  anti-migrant sentiment in UK have led to  apprehensiveness among students studying  abroad besides that students are wary of  countries such as France even though it  is regarded as a top study destination  since the major university programs in  this country are taught in French  language the next and most important  factor in selecting a country to study  abroad is budget students on a tight  budget always prioritize Germany but it  is not simple to get into any of the  public universities because competition  is fierce furthermore Nordic countries  are regarded as economical study  location for International students  countries such as Norway and Poland are  available to everyone irrespective of  their nationality  students will only have to pay for a  specialized courses in these countries  whereas there is no tuition fee in  Germany if you get selected by a public  university  finally the last factor to look into is  return on investment return on  investment is simple ratio that divides  the net profit or loss from an  investment by its cost because it is  expressed as a percentage you can  compare the effectiveness or  profitability of your investment in this  scenario one way to look at Roi is the  amount of time it takes to recoup your  investment in education  for Masters European institutions  generally have one year master's degree  whereas U.S institutions have two years  master's degree it is definitely less  expensive to study in Europe in the  present scenario Germany for example  should be the ideal choice if one is  looking at getting the maximum return on  his investment because Germany provides  pre-education even for international  students one more country that has  recently become very popular is Island  Ireland offers a one-year program and  has become the European capital of I.T  inspiring many students to look at the  country for higher education  to emphasize this point further consider  this scenario for MBA students doing a  one-year European MBA would get more  return for their bucks as they have  spent only one year courses fee plus  potential employment loss this is the  reason why inside MBA is rated the  highest on value for money versus other  prestigious schools like Harvard or  Stanford on that note let's discover the  top four countries for pursuing abroad  education based on the factors we have  just discovered  the fourth country on our list is  Australia Australia promotes Innovation  creativity and independent thinking  throughout its universities  International students in Australia  highlight that their education is  challenging fun and rewarding besides  that eight universities out of 39  Australian universities rank among top  100 institutes globally Australian  National University University of  Melbourne University of Sydney  University of New South Wales and  University of Queensland are the top  five universities in Australia now let's  talk about why we have listed Australia  at the fourth position the main reason  behind that is the budget associated  with education in Australia  the average tuition fee for  undergraduate programs in Australia is  around 24 000 Australian dollars which  turns out to be almost 18 048 US Dollars  similarly if you are looking to pursue a  postgraduate degree in Australia then  the average tuition cost is around 32  000 Australian dollars that's not the  end of expenses you'll have to think  about living expenses as well the  average monthly living expense in  Australia for one person is 3 800  Australian dollars if you convert this  number into U.S dollars it becomes  almost 3 000 USD that is a lot of money  aside from that here is an interesting  fact the cost of living in Australia is  almost 15 percent greater than the  America it ranks 10th among the most  expensive countries to live in living  both UK and USA behind  the reserve funds you'll have to keep in  a closed bank account are almost 21 000  Australian dollars which represents you  have the financial means to cover at  least one year's educational expenses in  Australia budget wise this is not the  ideal choice for students with financial  restrictions that is the reason why we  have Australia as the fourth contender  next up on our list is United Kingdom  as mentioned earlier 16 universities in  UK rank among top Global universities  the University of Oxford University of  Cambridge Imperial College London are  the top universities that rank among top  10 Global universities besides that  these colleges have been around since  the Middle Ages bearing a significant  history of world education that is why  the United Kingdom has been ranked  number one globally for the quality of  education and Facilities the UK has the  best educational system globally  comprised of undergraduate postgraduate  and doctoral degrees  ug courses are designed to help Learners  gain practical exposure after three  years of undergraduate courses Learners  can pursue a master's degree the  one-year Master's course offer more  in-depth study for particular subject  that makes Learners eligible for  high-paying jobs and promotions the next  factor is budget as you must know the UK  is one of the most expensive countries  to live in the tuition fee in UK lie  around an average of 13 000 50 euros  whereas living expenses are around 10  308 Euros that means the block account  fund for a Year's expense will be the  sum of both these figures which turns  out to be almost 26 000 US Dollars the  country that holds second rank on our  list is United States according to the  report of education.com the United  States has been ranked second worldwide  for the quality of Education  MIT Stanford Harvard the University of  Chicago and the University of  Pennsylvania are the top five American  universities ranking among the top 15  institutions globally  for decades the U.S has reigned Supreme  as the world's most popular study abroad  destination the country's prestigious  institutions dominate Global University  rankings attracting students from across  the world with an appetite for academic  excellence  according to the project Atlas report  1.2 million plus International students  reside in United States the reason  behind that is the immigration policies  of country and cultural Acceptance in  the U.S International students can stay  and work for 12 months after completing  their studies further students who go  for stem education this duration is 24  months Indians are the largest  beneficiary for H-1B visas more than 60  percent of these visas are issued to the  Indian Community which is a great deal  for the Indian Community  now coming to the budget to study in  America the living expenses and tuition  fee are quite higher here you'll have to  pay around 35 331 US Dollars on average  to get into the university program also  the average living cost is around 18 000  US Dollars which is quite high too  however many students prefer the USA  since the job opportunities here are  quite lucrative and as high as you can  get many students cite that they  fulfilled their Education Loans within  two to three years of time span this  indicates High Returns on investment in  mediocre time  on that note let's move towards the  first country on our list Germany  Germany has always been among the top  Global destinations for students across  the globe because the german-speaking  people have been an Inseparable part of  world's greatest invention in both Arts  and Sciences practically every academic  area has a long and exceptional Heritage  of success stories here in Germany  furthermore Germany has abolished all  tuition cost for both National and  international students making education  more accessible  the top five public institutions  offering pre-education in Germany a  Technical University of Munich  University of Heidelberg LMU Munich free  University Berlin and Humboldt  University there are 430 plus public  universities in Germany that offer  education at no cost these universities  will only charge you approximately 500  to 600 euros per semester for  administrative expenditure typically  referred to as semester contributions  these speeds cover contribution charges  travel expenses and student union fees  the next benefit of Germany as a study  destination is the lower block funds  these funds serve as proof that you have  the financial means to cover at least  one year's living expenses since there  is no tuition fee in Germany this amount  is lower you'll just have to show the  amount summing up your one-year living  expenses such as rent internet food Etc  considering inflation the mandatory  amount required in the block account for  studying in Germany as of January 1 2022  its Euros 10 332 for an entire year or  Euros 861 for a month candidate would  have to keep a little more than the said  amount as the bank could Levi a service  charge on the student opening block  account in Germany however you need not  to worry about the charges because  German law allows you to work for 20  hours a week and almost 120 full days in  a year you'll not require any type of  approval for this you can automatically  work for 20 hours a week the moment you  have National visa for a student plus a  remuneration is a beneficiary Factor  here you'll get 15 euros per hour of  your work also the master's program in  Germany are typically for one year which  means you'll only have to pay fees for  one year and later by launching and  acing your job hunt you can start  earning as well as fulfilling your  educational loans as you might know  Germany is the fourth largest economy in  the world after United States China and  Japan also it is the largest economy in  Eastern Europe continent because of that  there are plenty of jobs available for  international students with technical  expertise however to get the jobs you  you are required to have German language  proficiency be one level of language  proficiency is bare minimum before you  can look out for permanent job let's  talk about sectors that produce maximum  job opportunities in Germany the first  one is information technology as you  know the world is gravitating towards  complete virtualization since the covet  pandemic the requirement for it experts  in Germany has increased exponentially  according to the survey there are around  124 000 open jobs for ID Professionals  in Germany that's why it is at the top  of our list the next sector that  produces more jobs in Germany is  engineering particularly mechanical  engineering and automobile engineering  are the trail bridges that produce a  pool of job opportunities you can also  find abundant jobs related to  electronics Robotics and chemical  engineering sectors another sector that  has huge potential is Medical Science  Germany has always been a big  contributor to the global medical sector  so  you can definitely get jobs for  healthcare sector as well that's all we  have about the best countries to study  abroad however if you don't have the  required Capital support to launch your  International Journey we recommend you  to look out for Global PSW programs  available online  these programs can help you accelerate  your career in global market with the  least Financial requirements simple  learn offers one such Management program  in collaboration with IU Germany you can  now get access to the best that IU has  to offer study on campus build an  International Management career and get  an opportunity to work in Germany with  this master of Business Administration  MBA program in collaboration with IU  Germany and London South Bank University  lsba you can become a Global Management  industry leader furthermore after  successful completion of this course  you'll be able to launch a career in  German corporations with an 18-month  long post-study work visa here are few  highest paying job opportunities that  you can get in Germany after finishing  this accredited MBA program  the average base salary for finance  Professionals in Germany range around  almost 89 000 Euros which pan out to be  75 lakh rupees in India the best salary  for marketing professionals is almost 65  600 euros having an equivalence of 54  lakh Indian rupees the next MBA  specialization that is business  analytics also has fruitful salaries it  starts from 60 000 Euros the fourth one  is Operation and logistic management  profession  this profession can provide you with  salaries starting from a base pay of 72  000 Euros  and finally human resource Professionals  in Germany can earn from 50 000 Euros  having equivalence of 42 lakh Indian  rupees all these numbers mentioned above  are quite fruitful compared to the  salaries in other developing countries  so thinking about this program is  worthwhile that's all we have for today  thank you so much for watching this  video and stay tuned for more from  Simply learn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learned YouTube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here

